## Hidden Halo vs Visible Halo

The hidden halo sits beneath the centre stone, visible only from the side. The visible halo wraps around the centre stone from the top-down view. Both deliver tip protection, but the visual effect is different.

<table class="dc-custom-table"><thead><tr><th>Halo Type</th><th>Top-Down View</th><th>Side View</th><th>Price Range</th><th>What this means</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Visible halo</strong></td><td>Halo visible around centre</td><td>Halo visible under centre</td><td>$2,000–$5,985</td><td>Classic halo look. Maximum visual multiplier.</td></tr><tr class="highlight-row"><td><strong>Hidden halo</strong></td><td>Looks like solitaire</td><td>Halo visible beneath</td><td>$1,255–$3,040</td><td>Modern. Looks like solitaire from above.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Double halo</strong></td><td>Two halo rings visible</td><td>Both halos visible</td><td>$2,265–$5,985</td><td>Maximum visual carat. For 1ct–1.5ct centres.</td></tr><tr class="highlight-row"><td><strong>Micro-halo</strong></td><td>Thin halo visible</td><td>Thin halo visible</td><td>$1,430–$2,500</td><td>Subtle sparkle. Centre still dominates visually.</td></tr></tbody></table>

**Verdict:** Hidden halo for buyers who want "classic solitaire look with extra sparkle from the side." Visible halo for buyers who want "the halo to be the whole point." Double halo for buyers who want the biggest-looking ring at a given carat. Micro-halo for subtle buyers.

## Halo vs Solitaire vs Three-Stone for Marquise

A halo is one of three main setting families for marquise. The other two — solitaire and three-stone — change the maths. Quick comparison:

<table class="dc-custom-table"><thead><tr><th>Setting Family</th><th>Setting Cost</th><th>Tip Protection</th><th>Visual Multiplier</th><th>What this means</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Solitaire</strong></td><td>$790–$1,800</td><td>Depends on prongs</td><td>None</td><td>Classic look. See <a href="/marquise-solitaire-engagement-ring">solitaire guide</a>.</td></tr><tr class="highlight-row"><td><strong>Halo</strong></td><td>$1,255–$5,985</td><td>High (halo wraps belly)</td><td>1.5x visual carat</td><td>Our pick for 1ct-1.5ct centres.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Three-Stone</strong></td><td>$1,970–$4,790</td><td>Moderate</td><td>None (adds carat via sides)</td><td>Dramatic, meaningful. See <a href="/marquise-three-stone-engagement-ring">three-stone guide</a>.</td></tr><tr class="highlight-row"><td><strong>Hidden Halo</strong></td><td>$1,255–$3,040</td><td>Moderate (halo wraps under)</td><td>Minimal (side view only)</td><td>Solitaire on top, halo underneath. Modern pick.</td></tr></tbody></table>

**Verdict:** The halo wins on visual multiplier per dollar. The solitaire wins on classic look. The three-stone wins on meaning. For a buyer who wants "biggest possible stone look at smallest possible price," halo wins by a wide margin.

